  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amit Kumar vs The State Of Bihar on 9 March, 2015",
    "facts": "Petitioner apprehends his arrest in connection with G.O. Case No. 18 of 2013 registered for the offence punishable under Section 26(2) (1) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. According to prosecution case, some sweets were seized from the shop of the petitioner and in course of examination in Combined Food and Drug Laboratory, Agamkuan, Patna it was found that red and green beads were present in the sweet which were not permitted colour. The contention on behalf of the petitioner is that the shop from which the alleged seizure was made does not belong to the petitioner rather the brother of the petitioner is owner of the aforesaid shop. To fortify his contention, he drew my attention towards Annexure-2 to this petition.",
